window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b214-1627b49c1f1b0d3f.json"]={sha256:"1627b49c1f1b0d3f8f88a97e572fe6fc7021bf7e696c440dba7dfecf33917f55",value:{"id":"b214","title":"大迪克桑斯壩","titleEn":"Grande Dixence Dam","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以以大迪克桑斯重力壩高山集水與壩基監測學習為主線，先用高山集水與季節庫存與高壩投影水壓界定水力與構造條件，再將合力偏心與接觸、水化熱與拘束連結到高落差輸水與淨能量。公開高度與年代僅作案例背景，合成斷面不等於真實壩形，所有安全比值均非設計評定。 每單元以原創算例、量測與失效辨識共同檢查推論。","summaryEn":"This course develops studying Grande Dixence gravity action alpine collection and foundation monitoring through Alpine collection and seasonal storage and High dam projected hydrostatic load, then connects Resultant eccentricity and contact and Hydration heat and restraint to High-head conveyance and net energy. Public height and dates provide context only; synthetic sections are not the actual dam and calculated ratios are not design assessments. Each unit combines original calculation, measurement and failure diagnosis to test the inference.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-dams","subcategoryTitle":"世界水壩與水庫","subcategoryTitleEn":"World dams and reservoirs","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-dams","learningTags":["water","water-dams","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-dam","architectureNodes":[["高山集水與季節庫存","Alpine collection and seasonal storage"],["混凝土自重與質量","Concrete weight and mass"],["合力偏心與接觸","Resultant eccentricity and contact"],["水化熱與拘束","Hydration heat and restraint"],["高落差輸水與淨能量","High-head conveyance and net energy"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[0,3]],"diagram":{"type":"water-dam","labels":["高山集水與季節庫存","混凝土自重與質量","合力偏心與接觸","水化熱與拘束","高落差輸水與淨能量"],"labelsEn":["Alpine collection and seasonal storage","Concrete weight and mass","Resultant eccentricity and contact","Hydration heat and restraint","High-head conveyance and net energy"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合算例輸入全為教學假設，先檢查高山集水與季節庫存：SyntheticCollectedFlow=12 m3/s for20 days; collectedVolume=12*20*86400/1e6=20.736 million m3；再獨立檢查高壩投影水壓：SyntheticWaterDepth=180 m; unitWidth=1 m; hydrostaticForce=0.5*9.81*180**2=158922 kN per m width。敏感度：合成底面總下向力90000kN與摩擦係數0.7不變，揚力由20000增至30000kN，摩擦抗力由49000降至42000kN，減少14.29%；不能假設排水永久維持初始效果。 兩個結果須按各自量綱解釋，不能直接相加或當成完整設計。公開高度與年代僅作案例背景，合成斷面不等於真實壩形，所有安全比值均非設計評定。 將保持試段長度壓差一致並比較帷幕上下游孔壓作為獨立驗證，明確列出尚缺的現地輸入及其對結論的影響。","textEn":"Every input in this integrated example is a teaching assumption. First examine Alpine collection and seasonal storage: SyntheticCollectedFlow=12 m3/s for20 days; collectedVolume=12*20*86400/1e6=20.736 million m3. Independently examine High dam projected hydrostatic load: SyntheticWaterDepth=180 m; unitWidth=1 m; hydrostaticForce=0.5*9.81*180**2=158922 kN per m width. Sensitivity: with90000kN downward force and0.7 friction coefficient, raising uplift from20000 to30000kN reduces frictional resistance from49000 to42000kN, or14.29 percent. Drainage cannot be assumed permanently effective at its initial state. Interpret each result in its own dimensions rather than adding them or treating them as a complete design. Public height and dates provide context only; synthetic sections are not the actual dam and calculated ratios are not design assessments. Use the following independent check: Match interval length and pressure and compare heads on both sides of the curtain. Identify missing field inputs and state which conclusions depend on them.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b214-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「高山集水與季節庫存」與「高壩投影水壓」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Alpine collection and seasonal storage\" and \"High dam projected hydrostatic load\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b214-v15-01","title":"高山集水與季節庫存：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Alpine collection and seasonal storage: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「高山集水與季節庫存」如何影響大迪克桑斯壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alpine collection and seasonal storage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grande Dixence Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"大迪克桑斯系統將高山集水與蓄水發電連結，融雪、降雨與輸水設備共同限制可收集水量。流量積分只表示指定時窗的輸入，不代表全部都可用於發電；溢流、抽水耗能及生態放流需在共同水量邊界另列。 驗證時應將各支流取水與庫存變化對帳並區分抽水輸入與自然入流，並辨識以下失效情境：只加總取水量會漏掉輸水損失與非發電放流。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「高山集水與季節庫存」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Grande Dixence links alpine collection with storage and generation. Snowmelt, rainfall and conveyance capacity constrain captured water. Integrated flow describes one input window, not fully usable generating water; spills, pumping demand and environmental releases belong in the same accounting boundary. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Reconcile tributary collection with storage and distinguish pumped from natural inflow. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Summing collection alone omits conveyance losses and nongenerating releases. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alpine collection and seasonal storage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：SyntheticCollectedFlow=12 m3/s for20 days; collectedVolume=12*20*86400/1e6=20.736 million m3。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticCollectedFlow=12 m3/s for20 days; collectedVolume=12*20*86400/1e6=20.736 million m3.","failure":"常見誤解：「收集到的水量必定全部轉成可發電水量」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Every collected water volume necessarily becomes generating water\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「高山集水與季節庫存」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alpine collection and seasonal storage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-01-k1","title":"高山集水與季節庫存","titleEn":"Alpine collection and seasonal storage","text":"大迪克桑斯系統將高山集水與蓄水發電連結，融雪、降雨與輸水設備共同限制可收集水量。流量積分只表示指定時窗的輸入，不代表全部都可用於發電；溢流、抽水耗能及生態放流需在共同水量邊界另列。","textEn":"Grande Dixence links alpine collection with storage and generation. Snowmelt, rainfall and conveyance capacity constrain captured water.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：收集到的水量必定全部轉成可發電水量 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Every collected water volume necessarily becomes generating water Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高山集水與季節庫存」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Alpine collection and seasonal storage\" is correct?","options":["收集到的水量必定全部轉成可發電水量","大迪克桑斯系統將高山集水與蓄水發電連結，融雪、降雨與輸水設備共同限制可收集水量。","公開壩高就是任何工況下的實際水深"],"optionsEn":["Every collected water volume necessarily becomes generating water","Grande Dixence links alpine collection with storage and generation.","Published dam height equals actual water depth in every condition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"大迪克桑斯系統將高山集水與蓄水發電連結，融雪、降雨與輸水設備共同限制可收集水量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Grande Dixence links alpine collection with storage and generation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b214-v15-02","title":"高山集水與季節庫存：定量估算","titleEn":"Alpine collection and seasonal storage: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「高山集水與季節庫存」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alpine collection and seasonal storage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：SyntheticCollectedFlow=12 m3/s for20 days; collectedVolume=12*20*86400/1e6=20.736 million m3。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticCollectedFlow=12 m3/s for20 days; collectedVolume=12*20*86400/1e6=20.736 million m3. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將各支流取水與庫存變化對帳並區分抽水輸入與自然入流。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconcile tributary collection with storage and distinguish pumped from natural inflow.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：SyntheticCollectedFlow=12 m3/s for20 days; collectedVolume=12*20*86400/1e6=20.736 million m3。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticCollectedFlow=12 m3/s for20 days; collectedVolume=12*20*86400/1e6=20.736 million m3. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「高山集水與季節庫存」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Alpine collection and seasonal storage\", which statement holds?","options":["一個排水孔壓力低就代表整個底面揚力低","揚壓只影響抗浮而不影響滑動摩擦","原創教學假設：SyntheticCollectedFlow=12 m3/s for20 days; collectedVolume=12*20*86400/1e6=20.736 million m3。"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure at one drain proves low uplift across the entire base","Uplift affects flotation only and never sliding friction","Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticCollectedFlow=12 m3/s for20 days; collectedVolume=12*20*86400/1e6=20.736 million m3."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：SyntheticCollectedFlow=12 m3/s for20 days; collectedVolume=12*20*86400/1e6=20.736 million m3。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticCollectedFlow=12 m3/s for20 days; collectedVolume=12*20*86400/1e6=20.736 million m3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b214-v15-03","title":"高山集水與季節庫存：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Alpine collection and seasonal storage: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「高山集水與季節庫存」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alpine collection and seasonal storage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將各支流取水與庫存變化對帳並區分抽水輸入與自然入流。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只加總取水量會漏掉輸水損失與非發電放流」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconcile tributary collection with storage and distinguish pumped from natural inflow. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Summing collection alone omits conveyance losses and nongenerating releases. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以將各支流取水與庫存變化對帳並區分抽水輸入與自然入流作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只加總取水量會漏掉輸水損失與非發電放流，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Reconcile tributary collection with storage and distinguish pumped from natural inflow. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Summing collection alone omits conveyance losses and nongenerating releases. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：只加總取水量會漏掉輸水損失與非發電放流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Summing collection alone omits conveyance losses and nongenerating releases. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將各支流取水與庫存變化對帳並區分抽水輸入與自然入流。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只加總取水量會漏掉輸水損失與非發電放流」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Reconcile tributary collection with storage and distinguish pumped from natural inflow. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Summing collection alone omits conveyance losses and nongenerating releases. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以將各支流取水與庫存變化對帳並區分抽水輸入與自然入流作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只加總取水量會漏掉輸水損失與非發電放流，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Reconcile tributary collection with storage and distinguish pumped from natural inflow. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Summing collection alone omits conveyance losses and nongenerating releases. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「高山集水與季節庫存」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Alpine collection and seasonal storage\"?","options":["將各支流取水與庫存變化對帳並區分抽水輸入與自然入流。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","灌漿量越多就必定代表防滲效果越好"],"optionsEn":["Reconcile tributary collection with storage and distinguish pumped from natural inflow.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","More injected grout necessarily means better seepage control"],"answer":0,"explanation":"將各支流取水與庫存變化對帳並區分抽水輸入與自然入流。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconcile tributary collection with storage and distinguish pumped from natural inflow. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b214-v15-04","title":"高山集水與季節庫存：失效診斷","titleEn":"Alpine collection and seasonal storage: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「高山集水與季節庫存」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alpine collection and seasonal storage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只加總取水量會漏掉輸水損失與非發電放流。診斷時應採取以下查核：將各支流取水與庫存變化對帳並區分抽水輸入與自然入流，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Summing collection alone omits conveyance losses and nongenerating releases. Diagnose it by the following check: Reconcile tributary collection with storage and distinguish pumped from natural inflow. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「收集到的水量必定全部轉成可發電水量」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every collected water volume necessarily becomes generating water\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只加總取水量會漏掉輸水損失與非發電放流。診斷時應採取以下查核：將各支流取水與庫存變化對帳並區分抽水輸入與自然入流，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Summing collection alone omits conveyance losses and nongenerating releases. Diagnose it by the following check: Reconcile tributary collection with storage and distinguish pumped from natural inflow. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高山集水與季節庫存」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Alpine collection and seasonal storage\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只加總取水量會漏掉輸水損失與非發電放流。","公開壩高就是任何工況下的實際水深"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Summing collection alone omits conveyance losses and nongenerating releases.","Published dam height equals actual water depth in every condition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"只加總取水量會漏掉輸水損失與非發電放流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Summing collection alone omits conveyance losses and nongenerating releases. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b214-v15-05","title":"高壩投影水壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"High dam projected hydrostatic load: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「高壩投影水壓」如何影響大迪克桑斯壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “High dam projected hydrostatic load” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grande Dixence Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"重力壩以自身重量及地基作用抵抗水平水壓，水深增加使三角分布合力按平方成長。單寬投影式只是二維自由體的一項，壩體實際幾何、尾水與地震水動力需另列；不能以公共壩高直接替代運轉水深。 驗證時應以同時庫尾水位及實測斷面建立完整荷載圖，並辨識以下失效情境：把結構總高度當滿水深會錯置受壓範圍與力矩。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「高壩投影水壓」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A gravity dam resists horizontal water action through weight and foundation interaction. The triangular resultant grows with depth squared. A unit-width projection is one term in a two-dimensional free body; actual geometry, tailwater and seismic hydrodynamics remain separate, and public dam height is not operating depth. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Build the complete load diagram from simultaneous reservoir and tailwater levels and surveyed sections. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Using total structural height as water depth misplaces the loaded area and moment. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “High dam projected hydrostatic load” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：SyntheticWaterDepth=180 m; unitWidth=1 m; hydrostaticForce=0.5*9.81*180**2=158922 kN per m width。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticWaterDepth=180 m; unitWidth=1 m; hydrostaticForce=0.5*9.81*180**2=158922 kN per m width.","failure":"常見誤解：「公開壩高就是任何工況下的實際水深」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Published dam height equals actual water depth in every condition\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「高壩投影水壓」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “High dam projected hydrostatic load”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-05-k1","title":"高壩投影水壓","titleEn":"High dam projected hydrostatic load","text":"重力壩以自身重量及地基作用抵抗水平水壓，水深增加使三角分布合力按平方成長。單寬投影式只是二維自由體的一項，壩體實際幾何、尾水與地震水動力需另列；不能以公共壩高直接替代運轉水深。","textEn":"A gravity dam resists horizontal water action through weight and foundation interaction. The triangular resultant grows with depth squared.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：公開壩高就是任何工況下的實際水深 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Published dam height equals actual water depth in every condition Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高壩投影水壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"High dam projected hydrostatic load\" is correct?","options":["公開壩高就是任何工況下的實際水深","混凝土質量的噸數可以直接當作千牛頓重量","重力壩以自身重量及地基作用抵抗水平水壓，水深增加使三角分布合力按平方成長。"],"optionsEn":["Published dam height equals actual water depth in every condition","Concrete mass in tonnes can be used directly as weight in kilonewtons","A gravity dam resists horizontal water action through weight and foundation interaction."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重力壩以自身重量及地基作用抵抗水平水壓，水深增加使三角分布合力按平方成長。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A gravity dam resists horizontal water action through weight and foundation interaction. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b214-v15-06","title":"高壩投影水壓：定量估算","titleEn":"High dam projected hydrostatic load: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「高壩投影水壓」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “High dam projected hydrostatic load” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：SyntheticWaterDepth=180 m; unitWidth=1 m; hydrostaticForce=0.5*9.81*180**2=158922 kN per m width。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticWaterDepth=180 m; unitWidth=1 m; hydrostaticForce=0.5*9.81*180**2=158922 kN per m width. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以同時庫尾水位及實測斷面建立完整荷載圖。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build the complete load diagram from simultaneous reservoir and tailwater levels and surveyed sections.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：SyntheticWaterDepth=180 m; unitWidth=1 m; hydrostaticForce=0.5*9.81*180**2=158922 kN per m width。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticWaterDepth=180 m; unitWidth=1 m; hydrostaticForce=0.5*9.81*180**2=158922 kN per m width. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「高壩投影水壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"High dam projected hydrostatic load\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：SyntheticWaterDepth=180 m; unitWidth=1 m; hydrostaticForce=0.5*9.81*180**2=158922 kN per m width。","合力在底面內就保證全底面始終受壓","完全拘束彈性熱應力就是所有實際位置的應力"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticWaterDepth=180 m; unitWidth=1 m; hydrostaticForce=0.5*9.81*180**2=158922 kN per m width.","A resultant anywhere inside the base guarantees compression over the entire base","Fully restrained elastic thermal stress equals stress at every actual location"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：SyntheticWaterDepth=180 m; unitWidth=1 m; hydrostaticForce=0.5*9.81*180**2=158922 kN per m width。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticWaterDepth=180 m; unitWidth=1 m; hydrostaticForce=0.5*9.81*180**2=158922 kN per m width. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b214-v15-07","title":"高壩投影水壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"High dam projected hydrostatic load: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「高壩投影水壓」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “High dam projected hydrostatic load” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以同時庫尾水位及實測斷面建立完整荷載圖。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把結構總高度當滿水深會錯置受壓範圍與力矩」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build the complete load diagram from simultaneous reservoir and tailwater levels and surveyed sections. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using total structural height as water depth misplaces the loaded area and moment. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以同時庫尾水位及實測斷面建立完整荷載圖作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把結構總高度當滿水深會錯置受壓範圍與力矩，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Build the complete load diagram from simultaneous reservoir and tailwater levels and surveyed sections. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using total structural height as water depth misplaces the loaded area and moment. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：把結構總高度當滿水深會錯置受壓範圍與力矩。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using total structural height as water depth misplaces the loaded area and moment. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同時庫尾水位及實測斷面建立完整荷載圖。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把結構總高度當滿水深會錯置受壓範圍與力矩」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Build the complete load diagram from simultaneous reservoir and tailwater levels and surveyed sections. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using total structural height as water depth misplaces the loaded area and moment. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以同時庫尾水位及實測斷面建立完整荷載圖作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把結構總高度當滿水深會錯置受壓範圍與力矩，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Build the complete load diagram from simultaneous reservoir and tailwater levels and surveyed sections. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using total structural height as water depth misplaces the loaded area and moment. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「高壩投影水壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"High dam projected hydrostatic load\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以同時庫尾水位及實測斷面建立完整荷載圖。","垂線差值必定就是壩體絕對地理位移"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Build the complete load diagram from simultaneous reservoir and tailwater levels and surveyed sections.","A plumb-line difference necessarily equals absolute geographic dam movement"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以同時庫尾水位及實測斷面建立完整荷載圖。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build the complete load diagram from simultaneous reservoir and tailwater levels and surveyed sections. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b214-v15-08","title":"高壩投影水壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"High dam projected hydrostatic load: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「高壩投影水壓」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “High dam projected hydrostatic load” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把結構總高度當滿水深會錯置受壓範圍與力矩。診斷時應採取以下查核：以同時庫尾水位及實測斷面建立完整荷載圖，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using total structural height as water depth misplaces the loaded area and moment. Diagnose it by the following check: Build the complete load diagram from simultaneous reservoir and tailwater levels and surveyed sections. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「公開壩高就是任何工況下的實際水深」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Published dam height equals actual water depth in every condition\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把結構總高度當滿水深會錯置受壓範圍與力矩。診斷時應採取以下查核：以同時庫尾水位及實測斷面建立完整荷載圖，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Using total structural height as water depth misplaces the loaded area and moment. Diagnose it by the following check: Build the complete load diagram from simultaneous reservoir and tailwater levels and surveyed sections. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高壩投影水壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"High dam projected hydrostatic load\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","混凝土質量的噸數可以直接當作千牛頓重量","把結構總高度當滿水深會錯置受壓範圍與力矩。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Concrete mass in tonnes can be used directly as weight in kilonewtons","Using total structural height as water depth misplaces the loaded area and moment."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把結構總高度當滿水深會錯置受壓範圍與力矩。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using total structural height as water depth misplaces the loaded area and moment. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b214-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「混凝土自重與質量」與「底面揚力與排水」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Concrete weight and mass\" and \"Base uplift and drainage\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b214-v15-09","title":"混凝土自重與質量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Concrete weight and mass: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「混凝土自重與質量」如何影響大迪克桑斯壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Concrete weight and mass” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grande Dixence Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"壩體混凝土的密度與體積先給質量，再乘重力才得到重量，兩者不可混用。合成單寬斷面自重須使用斷面面積與厚度，廊道和空洞另扣；重心位置同樣重要，因其決定抵抗力矩而不只總重量。 驗證時應核對廊道扣除與重心位置並分別列出質量及重量單位，並辨識以下失效情境：漏扣大廊道或錯置重心會同時影響自重與穩定力矩。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「混凝土自重與質量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Density and volume yield mass; multiplying by gravity yields weight. A synthetic unit-width section needs area and thickness, with galleries and voids deducted. The centroid matters as much as total weight because it sets the resisting moment rather than merely the downward force. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Check gallery deductions and centroid and distinguish mass units from force units. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Omitted galleries or a misplaced centroid alter weight and stability moments. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Concrete weight and mass” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：SyntheticSectionArea=12000 m2; width=1 m; concreteDensity=2400 kg/m3; weight=12000*1*2400*9.81/1000=282528 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticSectionArea=12000 m2; width=1 m; concreteDensity=2400 kg/m3; weight=12000*1*2400*9.81/1000=282528 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土質量的噸數可以直接當作千牛頓重量」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Concrete mass in tonnes can be used directly as weight in kilonewtons\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「混凝土自重與質量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Concrete weight and mass”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-09-k1","title":"混凝土自重與質量","titleEn":"Concrete weight and mass","text":"壩體混凝土的密度與體積先給質量，再乘重力才得到重量，兩者不可混用。合成單寬斷面自重須使用斷面面積與厚度，廊道和空洞另扣；重心位置同樣重要，因其決定抵抗力矩而不只總重量。","textEn":"Density and volume yield mass; multiplying by gravity yields weight. A synthetic unit-width section needs area and thickness, with galleries and voids deducted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土質量的噸數可以直接當作千牛頓重量 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Concrete mass in tonnes can be used directly as weight in kilonewtons Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「混凝土自重與質量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Concrete weight and mass\" is correct?","options":["壩體混凝土的密度與體積先給質量，再乘重力才得到重量，兩者不可混用。","混凝土質量的噸數可以直接當作千牛頓重量","一個排水孔壓力低就代表整個底面揚力低"],"optionsEn":["Density and volume yield mass; multiplying by gravity yields weight.","Concrete mass in tonnes can be used directly as weight in kilonewtons","Low pressure at one drain proves low uplift across the entire base"],"answer":0,"explanation":"壩體混凝土的密度與體積先給質量，再乘重力才得到重量，兩者不可混用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Density and volume yield mass; multiplying by gravity yields weight. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b214-v15-10","title":"混凝土自重與質量：定量估算","titleEn":"Concrete weight and mass: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「混凝土自重與質量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Concrete weight and mass” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：SyntheticSectionArea=12000 m2; width=1 m; concreteDensity=2400 kg/m3; weight=12000*1*2400*9.81/1000=282528 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticSectionArea=12000 m2; width=1 m; concreteDensity=2400 kg/m3; weight=12000*1*2400*9.81/1000=282528 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對廊道扣除與重心位置並分別列出質量及重量單位。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check gallery deductions and centroid and distinguish mass units from force units.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：SyntheticSectionArea=12000 m2; width=1 m; concreteDensity=2400 kg/m3; weight=12000*1*2400*9.81/1000=282528 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticSectionArea=12000 m2; width=1 m; concreteDensity=2400 kg/m3; weight=12000*1*2400*9.81/1000=282528 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「混凝土自重與質量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Concrete weight and mass\", which statement holds?","options":["揚壓只影響抗浮而不影響滑動摩擦","原創教學假設：SyntheticSectionArea=12000 m2; width=1 m; concreteDensity=2400 kg/m3; weight=12000*1*2400*9.81/1000=282528 kN。","灌漿量越多就必定代表防滲效果越好"],"optionsEn":["Uplift affects flotation only and never sliding friction","Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticSectionArea=12000 m2; width=1 m; concreteDensity=2400 kg/m3; weight=12000*1*2400*9.81/1000=282528 kN.","More injected grout necessarily means better seepage control"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：SyntheticSectionArea=12000 m2; width=1 m; concreteDensity=2400 kg/m3; weight=12000*1*2400*9.81/1000=282528 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticSectionArea=12000 m2; width=1 m; concreteDensity=2400 kg/m3; weight=12000*1*2400*9.81/1000=282528 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b214-v15-11","title":"混凝土自重與質量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Concrete weight and mass: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「混凝土自重與質量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Concrete weight and mass” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對廊道扣除與重心位置並分別列出質量及重量單位。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「漏扣大廊道或錯置重心會同時影響自重與穩定力矩」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check gallery deductions and centroid and distinguish mass units from force units. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Omitted galleries or a misplaced centroid alter weight and stability moments. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以核對廊道扣除與重心位置並分別列出質量及重量單位作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對漏扣大廊道或錯置重心會同時影響自重與穩定力矩，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check gallery deductions and centroid and distinguish mass units from force units. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Omitted galleries or a misplaced centroid alter weight and stability moments. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：漏扣大廊道或錯置重心會同時影響自重與穩定力矩。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitted galleries or a misplaced centroid alter weight and stability moments. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對廊道扣除與重心位置並分別列出質量及重量單位。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「漏扣大廊道或錯置重心會同時影響自重與穩定力矩」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Check gallery deductions and centroid and distinguish mass units from force units. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Omitted galleries or a misplaced centroid alter weight and stability moments. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以核對廊道扣除與重心位置並分別列出質量及重量單位作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對漏扣大廊道或錯置重心會同時影響自重與穩定力矩，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check gallery deductions and centroid and distinguish mass units from force units. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Omitted galleries or a misplaced centroid alter weight and stability moments. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「混凝土自重與質量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Concrete weight and mass\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","壩高就是整個高山水電系統的總發電落差","核對廊道扣除與重心位置並分別列出質量及重量單位。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Dam height equals the full generating head of an alpine scheme","Check gallery deductions and centroid and distinguish mass units from force units."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對廊道扣除與重心位置並分別列出質量及重量單位。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check gallery deductions and centroid and distinguish mass units from force units. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b214-v15-12","title":"混凝土自重與質量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Concrete weight and mass: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「混凝土自重與質量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Concrete weight and mass” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏扣大廊道或錯置重心會同時影響自重與穩定力矩。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對廊道扣除與重心位置並分別列出質量及重量單位，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitted galleries or a misplaced centroid alter weight and stability moments. Diagnose it by the following check: Check gallery deductions and centroid and distinguish mass units from force units. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土質量的噸數可以直接當作千牛頓重量」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Concrete mass in tonnes can be used directly as weight in kilonewtons\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏扣大廊道或錯置重心會同時影響自重與穩定力矩。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對廊道扣除與重心位置並分別列出質量及重量單位，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Omitted galleries or a misplaced centroid alter weight and stability moments. Diagnose it by the following check: Check gallery deductions and centroid and distinguish mass units from force units. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「混凝土自重與質量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Concrete weight and mass\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["漏扣大廊道或錯置重心會同時影響自重與穩定力矩。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","一個排水孔壓力低就代表整個底面揚力低"],"optionsEn":["Omitted galleries or a misplaced centroid alter weight and stability moments.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Low pressure at one drain proves low uplift across the entire base"],"answer":0,"explanation":"漏扣大廊道或錯置重心會同時影響自重與穩定力矩。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitted galleries or a misplaced centroid alter weight and stability moments. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b214-v15-13","title":"底面揚力與排水：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Base uplift and drainage: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「底面揚力與排水」如何影響大迪克桑斯壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Base uplift and drainage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grande Dixence Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"底面孔壓降低有效下向接觸力，防滲帷幕與排水需要分別檢查。線性水頭分布僅為明示假設，排水孔附近及節理連通可使實際分布不線性；不能只測單一孔壓就推定整個底面揚力，還需監測排水能力。 驗證時應沿底面廊道孔壓與排水流量核對假設分布，並辨識以下失效情境：排水堵塞會讓既有線性低壓假設失去依據。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「底面揚力與排水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Base pressure reduces effective downward contact. Grout curtains and drains need distinct checks. A linear head profile is an explicit assumption; drains and connected joints can make the real distribution nonlinear. One pressure reading cannot determine total uplift, so monitor pressure distribution and drainage performance together. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare gallery piezometers and drainage flow with the assumed base-pressure profile. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Drain blockage invalidates an assumed low-pressure profile. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Base uplift and drainage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Linear base head: upstream=100 m; downstream=20 m; baseWidth=80 m; stripWidth=1 m; uplift=9.81*(100+20)/2*80=47088 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Linear base head: upstream=100 m; downstream=20 m; baseWidth=80 m; stripWidth=1 m; uplift=9.81*(100+20)/2*80=47088 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「一個排水孔壓力低就代表整個底面揚力低」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Low pressure at one drain proves low uplift across the entire base\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「底面揚力與排水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Base uplift and drainage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-13-k1","title":"底面揚力與排水","titleEn":"Base uplift and drainage","text":"底面孔壓降低有效下向接觸力，防滲帷幕與排水需要分別檢查。線性水頭分布僅為明示假設，排水孔附近及節理連通可使實際分布不線性；不能只測單一孔壓就推定整個底面揚力，還需監測排水能力。","textEn":"Base pressure reduces effective downward contact. Grout curtains and drains need distinct checks.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：一個排水孔壓力低就代表整個底面揚力低 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Low pressure at one drain proves low uplift across the entire base Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「底面揚力與排水」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Base uplift and drainage\" is correct?","options":["一個排水孔壓力低就代表整個底面揚力低","底面孔壓降低有效下向接觸力，防滲帷幕與排水需要分別檢查。","合力在底面內就保證全底面始終受壓"],"optionsEn":["Low pressure at one drain proves low uplift across the entire base","Base pressure reduces effective downward contact.","A resultant anywhere inside the base guarantees compression over the entire base"],"answer":1,"explanation":"底面孔壓降低有效下向接觸力，防滲帷幕與排水需要分別檢查。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Base pressure reduces effective downward contact. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b214-v15-14","title":"底面揚力與排水：定量估算","titleEn":"Base uplift and drainage: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「底面揚力與排水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Base uplift and drainage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Linear base head: upstream=100 m; downstream=20 m; baseWidth=80 m; stripWidth=1 m; uplift=9.81*(100+20)/2*80=47088 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Linear base head: upstream=100 m; downstream=20 m; baseWidth=80 m; stripWidth=1 m; uplift=9.81*(100+20)/2*80=47088 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿底面廊道孔壓與排水流量核對假設分布。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare gallery piezometers and drainage flow with the assumed base-pressure profile.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Linear base head: upstream=100 m; downstream=20 m; baseWidth=80 m; stripWidth=1 m; uplift=9.81*(100+20)/2*80=47088 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Linear base head: upstream=100 m; downstream=20 m; baseWidth=80 m; stripWidth=1 m; uplift=9.81*(100+20)/2*80=47088 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「底面揚力與排水」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Base uplift and drainage\", which statement holds?","options":["完全拘束彈性熱應力就是所有實際位置的應力","垂線差值必定就是壩體絕對地理位移","原創教學假設：Linear base head: upstream=100 m; downstream=20 m; baseWidth=80 m; stripWidth=1 m; uplift=9.81*(100+20)/2*80=47088 kN。"],"optionsEn":["Fully restrained elastic thermal stress equals stress at every actual location","A plumb-line difference necessarily equals absolute geographic dam movement","Original teaching assumptions: Linear base head: upstream=100 m; downstream=20 m; baseWidth=80 m; stripWidth=1 m; uplift=9.81*(100+20)/2*80=47088 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Linear base head: upstream=100 m; downstream=20 m; baseWidth=80 m; stripWidth=1 m; uplift=9.81*(100+20)/2*80=47088 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Linear base head: upstream=100 m; downstream=20 m; baseWidth=80 m; stripWidth=1 m; uplift=9.81*(100+20)/2*80=47088 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b214-v15-15","title":"底面揚力與排水：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Base uplift and drainage: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「底面揚力與排水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Base uplift and drainage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿底面廊道孔壓與排水流量核對假設分布。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「排水堵塞會讓既有線性低壓假設失去依據」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare gallery piezometers and drainage flow with the assumed base-pressure profile. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Drain blockage invalidates an assumed low-pressure profile. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以沿底面廊道孔壓與排水流量核對假設分布作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對排水堵塞會讓既有線性低壓假設失去依據，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare gallery piezometers and drainage flow with the assumed base-pressure profile. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Drain blockage invalidates an assumed low-pressure profile. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：排水堵塞會讓既有線性低壓假設失去依據。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Drain blockage invalidates an assumed low-pressure profile. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿底面廊道孔壓與排水流量核對假設分布。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「排水堵塞會讓既有線性低壓假設失去依據」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare gallery piezometers and drainage flow with the assumed base-pressure profile. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Drain blockage invalidates an assumed low-pressure profile. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以沿底面廊道孔壓與排水流量核對假設分布作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對排水堵塞會讓既有線性低壓假設失去依據，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare gallery piezometers and drainage flow with the assumed base-pressure profile. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Drain blockage invalidates an assumed low-pressure profile. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「底面揚力與排水」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Base uplift and drainage\"?","options":["沿底面廊道孔壓與排水流量核對假設分布。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","收集到的水量必定全部轉成可發電水量"],"optionsEn":["Compare gallery piezometers and drainage flow with the assumed base-pressure profile.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Every collected water volume necessarily becomes generating water"],"answer":0,"explanation":"沿底面廊道孔壓與排水流量核對假設分布。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare gallery piezometers and drainage flow with the assumed base-pressure profile. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b214-v15-16","title":"底面揚力與排水：失效診斷","titleEn":"Base uplift and drainage: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「底面揚力與排水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Base uplift and drainage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"排水堵塞會讓既有線性低壓假設失去依據。診斷時應採取以下查核：沿底面廊道孔壓與排水流量核對假設分布，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Drain blockage invalidates an assumed low-pressure profile. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare gallery piezometers and drainage flow with the assumed base-pressure profile. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「一個排水孔壓力低就代表整個底面揚力低」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Low pressure at one drain proves low uplift across the entire base\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"排水堵塞會讓既有線性低壓假設失去依據。診斷時應採取以下查核：沿底面廊道孔壓與排水流量核對假設分布，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Drain blockage invalidates an assumed low-pressure profile. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare gallery piezometers and drainage flow with the assumed base-pressure profile. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「底面揚力與排水」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Base uplift and drainage\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","排水堵塞會讓既有線性低壓假設失去依據。","合力在底面內就保證全底面始終受壓"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Drain blockage invalidates an assumed low-pressure profile.","A resultant anywhere inside the base guarantees compression over the entire base"],"answer":1,"explanation":"排水堵塞會讓既有線性低壓假設失去依據。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Drain blockage invalidates an assumed low-pressure profile. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b214-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「合力偏心與接觸」與「抗滑摩擦與揚壓」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Resultant eccentricity and contact\" and \"Sliding friction and uplift\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b214-v15-17","title":"合力偏心與接觸：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Resultant eccentricity and contact: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「合力偏心與接觸」如何影響大迪克桑斯壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Resultant eccentricity and contact” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grande Dixence Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"單寬底面合力的偏心決定線彈性接觸壓力分布，核心範圍判斷須明示底面不能承拉或可承拉的模型。矩形全接觸公式在算出拉應力時已提示假設可能失效，不能保留負接觸壓力繼續當真實地基反力。 驗證時應以完整荷載力矩求合力位置並核對接觸模型是否允許拉力，並辨識以下失效情境：超出全接觸適用範圍仍用線性式會錯估壓縮區。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「合力偏心與接觸」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Resultant eccentricity controls the linear base-pressure distribution. State whether tension can be transferred. A full-contact rectangular formula that predicts tension signals a possible breakdown of its own assumption; negative contact pressure should not simply be retained as a real foundation reaction. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Locate the resultant from all moments and check whether the contact model permits tension. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Using full-contact equations beyond their range misstates the compressed area. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Resultant eccentricity and contact” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：SyntheticBaseWidth=60 m; resultantEccentricity=8 m; middleThirdLimit=60/6=10 m; geometricMargin=10-8=2 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticBaseWidth=60 m; resultantEccentricity=8 m; middleThirdLimit=60/6=10 m; geometricMargin=10-8=2 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「合力在底面內就保證全底面始終受壓」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A resultant anywhere inside the base guarantees compression over the entire base\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「合力偏心與接觸」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Resultant eccentricity and contact”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-17-k1","title":"合力偏心與接觸","titleEn":"Resultant eccentricity and contact","text":"單寬底面合力的偏心決定線彈性接觸壓力分布，核心範圍判斷須明示底面不能承拉或可承拉的模型。矩形全接觸公式在算出拉應力時已提示假設可能失效，不能保留負接觸壓力繼續當真實地基反力。","textEn":"Resultant eccentricity controls the linear base-pressure distribution. State whether tension can be transferred.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：合力在底面內就保證全底面始終受壓 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A resultant anywhere inside the base guarantees compression over the entire base Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「合力偏心與接觸」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Resultant eccentricity and contact\" is correct?","options":["合力在底面內就保證全底面始終受壓","揚壓只影響抗浮而不影響滑動摩擦","單寬底面合力的偏心決定線彈性接觸壓力分布，核心範圍判斷須明示底面不能承拉或可承拉的模型。"],"optionsEn":["A resultant anywhere inside the base guarantees compression over the entire base","Uplift affects flotation only and never sliding friction","Resultant eccentricity controls the linear base-pressure distribution."],"answer":2,"explanation":"單寬底面合力的偏心決定線彈性接觸壓力分布，核心範圍判斷須明示底面不能承拉或可承拉的模型。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Resultant eccentricity controls the linear base-pressure distribution. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b214-v15-18","title":"合力偏心與接觸：定量估算","titleEn":"Resultant eccentricity and contact: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「合力偏心與接觸」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Resultant eccentricity and contact” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：SyntheticBaseWidth=60 m; resultantEccentricity=8 m; middleThirdLimit=60/6=10 m; geometricMargin=10-8=2 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticBaseWidth=60 m; resultantEccentricity=8 m; middleThirdLimit=60/6=10 m; geometricMargin=10-8=2 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以完整荷載力矩求合力位置並核對接觸模型是否允許拉力。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Locate the resultant from all moments and check whether the contact model permits tension.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：SyntheticBaseWidth=60 m; resultantEccentricity=8 m; middleThirdLimit=60/6=10 m; geometricMargin=10-8=2 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticBaseWidth=60 m; resultantEccentricity=8 m; middleThirdLimit=60/6=10 m; geometricMargin=10-8=2 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「合力偏心與接觸」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Resultant eccentricity and contact\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：SyntheticBaseWidth=60 m; resultantEccentricity=8 m; middleThirdLimit=60/6=10 m; geometricMargin=10-8=2 m。","灌漿量越多就必定代表防滲效果越好","壩高就是整個高山水電系統的總發電落差"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticBaseWidth=60 m; resultantEccentricity=8 m; middleThirdLimit=60/6=10 m; geometricMargin=10-8=2 m.","More injected grout necessarily means better seepage control","Dam height equals the full generating head of an alpine scheme"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：SyntheticBaseWidth=60 m; resultantEccentricity=8 m; middleThirdLimit=60/6=10 m; geometricMargin=10-8=2 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticBaseWidth=60 m; resultantEccentricity=8 m; middleThirdLimit=60/6=10 m; geometricMargin=10-8=2 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b214-v15-19","title":"合力偏心與接觸：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Resultant eccentricity and contact: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「合力偏心與接觸」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Resultant eccentricity and contact” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以完整荷載力矩求合力位置並核對接觸模型是否允許拉力。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「超出全接觸適用範圍仍用線性式會錯估壓縮區」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Locate the resultant from all moments and check whether the contact model permits tension. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using full-contact equations beyond their range misstates the compressed area. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以完整荷載力矩求合力位置並核對接觸模型是否允許拉力作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對超出全接觸適用範圍仍用線性式會錯估壓縮區，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Locate the resultant from all moments and check whether the contact model permits tension. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using full-contact equations beyond their range misstates the compressed area. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：超出全接觸適用範圍仍用線性式會錯估壓縮區。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using full-contact equations beyond their range misstates the compressed area. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以完整荷載力矩求合力位置並核對接觸模型是否允許拉力。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「超出全接觸適用範圍仍用線性式會錯估壓縮區」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Locate the resultant from all moments and check whether the contact model permits tension. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using full-contact equations beyond their range misstates the compressed area. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以完整荷載力矩求合力位置並核對接觸模型是否允許拉力作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對超出全接觸適用範圍仍用線性式會錯估壓縮區，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Locate the resultant from all moments and check whether the contact model permits tension. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using full-contact equations beyond their range misstates the compressed area. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「合力偏心與接觸」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Resultant eccentricity and contact\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以完整荷載力矩求合力位置並核對接觸模型是否允許拉力。","公開壩高就是任何工況下的實際水深"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Locate the resultant from all moments and check whether the contact model permits tension.","Published dam height equals actual water depth in every condition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以完整荷載力矩求合力位置並核對接觸模型是否允許拉力。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Locate the resultant from all moments and check whether the contact model permits tension. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b214-v15-20","title":"合力偏心與接觸：失效診斷","titleEn":"Resultant eccentricity and contact: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「合力偏心與接觸」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Resultant eccentricity and contact” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"超出全接觸適用範圍仍用線性式會錯估壓縮區。診斷時應採取以下查核：以完整荷載力矩求合力位置並核對接觸模型是否允許拉力，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using full-contact equations beyond their range misstates the compressed area. Diagnose it by the following check: Locate the resultant from all moments and check whether the contact model permits tension. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「合力在底面內就保證全底面始終受壓」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A resultant anywhere inside the base guarantees compression over the entire base\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"超出全接觸適用範圍仍用線性式會錯估壓縮區。診斷時應採取以下查核：以完整荷載力矩求合力位置並核對接觸模型是否允許拉力，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Using full-contact equations beyond their range misstates the compressed area. Diagnose it by the following check: Locate the resultant from all moments and check whether the contact model permits tension. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「合力偏心與接觸」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Resultant eccentricity and contact\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","揚壓只影響抗浮而不影響滑動摩擦","超出全接觸適用範圍仍用線性式會錯估壓縮區。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Uplift affects flotation only and never sliding friction","Using full-contact equations beyond their range misstates the compressed area."],"answer":2,"explanation":"超出全接觸適用範圍仍用線性式會錯估壓縮區。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using full-contact equations beyond their range misstates the compressed area. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b214-v15-21","title":"抗滑摩擦與揚壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Sliding friction and uplift: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「抗滑摩擦與揚壓」如何影響大迪克桑斯壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sliding friction and uplift” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grande Dixence Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"摩擦抗力取決於有效正力而非總自重，揚壓、地震與不同荷載組合會改變可用接觸。無黏聚簡式只估一項抗力，不能代表含節理岩體的完整穩定；接觸面粗糙、剪脹及強度退化需由適當試驗與分析建立。 驗證時應核對揚壓量測與接觸剪力試驗並分列各荷載組合，並辨識以下失效情境：用總自重計摩擦會高估有揚壓時的抗滑能力。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「抗滑摩擦與揚壓」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Friction depends on effective normal force rather than gross weight. Uplift and load combinations alter contact. A cohesionless expression estimates one resistance component, not complete stability in jointed rock; roughness, dilation and degradation require suitable testing and analysis before using a strength parameter. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Check measured uplift and interface shear testing and list load combinations separately. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Using gross weight for friction overstates resistance when uplift acts. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sliding friction and uplift” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：totalDownwardForce=90000 kN; uplift=20000 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.7; frictionResistance=(90000-20000)*0.7=49000 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: totalDownwardForce=90000 kN; uplift=20000 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.7; frictionResistance=(90000-20000)*0.7=49000 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「揚壓只影響抗浮而不影響滑動摩擦」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uplift affects flotation only and never sliding friction\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「抗滑摩擦與揚壓」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sliding friction and uplift”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-21-k1","title":"抗滑摩擦與揚壓","titleEn":"Sliding friction and uplift","text":"摩擦抗力取決於有效正力而非總自重，揚壓、地震與不同荷載組合會改變可用接觸。無黏聚簡式只估一項抗力，不能代表含節理岩體的完整穩定；接觸面粗糙、剪脹及強度退化需由適當試驗與分析建立。","textEn":"Friction depends on effective normal force rather than gross weight. Uplift and load combinations alter contact.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：揚壓只影響抗浮而不影響滑動摩擦 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uplift affects flotation only and never sliding friction Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「抗滑摩擦與揚壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sliding friction and uplift\" is correct?","options":["摩擦抗力取決於有效正力而非總自重，揚壓、地震與不同荷載組合會改變可用接觸。","揚壓只影響抗浮而不影響滑動摩擦","完全拘束彈性熱應力就是所有實際位置的應力"],"optionsEn":["Friction depends on effective normal force rather than gross weight.","Uplift affects flotation only and never sliding friction","Fully restrained elastic thermal stress equals stress at every actual location"],"answer":0,"explanation":"摩擦抗力取決於有效正力而非總自重，揚壓、地震與不同荷載組合會改變可用接觸。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Friction depends on effective normal force rather than gross weight. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b214-v15-22","title":"抗滑摩擦與揚壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Sliding friction and uplift: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「抗滑摩擦與揚壓」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sliding friction and uplift” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：totalDownwardForce=90000 kN; uplift=20000 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.7; frictionResistance=(90000-20000)*0.7=49000 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: totalDownwardForce=90000 kN; uplift=20000 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.7; frictionResistance=(90000-20000)*0.7=49000 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對揚壓量測與接觸剪力試驗並分列各荷載組合。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check measured uplift and interface shear testing and list load combinations separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：totalDownwardForce=90000 kN; uplift=20000 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.7; frictionResistance=(90000-20000)*0.7=49000 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: totalDownwardForce=90000 kN; uplift=20000 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.7; frictionResistance=(90000-20000)*0.7=49000 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「抗滑摩擦與揚壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sliding friction and uplift\", which statement holds?","options":["垂線差值必定就是壩體絕對地理位移","原創教學假設：totalDownwardForce=90000 kN; uplift=20000 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.7; frictionResistance=(90000-20000)*0.7=49000 kN。","收集到的水量必定全部轉成可發電水量"],"optionsEn":["A plumb-line difference necessarily equals absolute geographic dam movement","Original teaching assumptions: totalDownwardForce=90000 kN; uplift=20000 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.7; frictionResistance=(90000-20000)*0.7=49000 kN.","Every collected water volume necessarily becomes generating water"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：totalDownwardForce=90000 kN; uplift=20000 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.7; frictionResistance=(90000-20000)*0.7=49000 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: totalDownwardForce=90000 kN; uplift=20000 kN; frictionCoefficient=0.7; frictionResistance=(90000-20000)*0.7=49000 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b214-v15-23","title":"抗滑摩擦與揚壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Sliding friction and uplift: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「抗滑摩擦與揚壓」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sliding friction and uplift” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對揚壓量測與接觸剪力試驗並分列各荷載組合。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「用總自重計摩擦會高估有揚壓時的抗滑能力」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check measured uplift and interface shear testing and list load combinations separately. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using gross weight for friction overstates resistance when uplift acts. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以核對揚壓量測與接觸剪力試驗並分列各荷載組合作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對用總自重計摩擦會高估有揚壓時的抗滑能力，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check measured uplift and interface shear testing and list load combinations separately. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using gross weight for friction overstates resistance when uplift acts. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：用總自重計摩擦會高估有揚壓時的抗滑能力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using gross weight for friction overstates resistance when uplift acts. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對揚壓量測與接觸剪力試驗並分列各荷載組合。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「用總自重計摩擦會高估有揚壓時的抗滑能力」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Check measured uplift and interface shear testing and list load combinations separately. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Using gross weight for friction overstates resistance when uplift acts. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以核對揚壓量測與接觸剪力試驗並分列各荷載組合作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對用總自重計摩擦會高估有揚壓時的抗滑能力，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check measured uplift and interface shear testing and list load combinations separately. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Using gross weight for friction overstates resistance when uplift acts. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「抗滑摩擦與揚壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sliding friction and uplift\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","混凝土質量的噸數可以直接當作千牛頓重量","核對揚壓量測與接觸剪力試驗並分列各荷載組合。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Concrete mass in tonnes can be used directly as weight in kilonewtons","Check measured uplift and interface shear testing and list load combinations separately."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對揚壓量測與接觸剪力試驗並分列各荷載組合。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check measured uplift and interface shear testing and list load combinations separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b214-v15-24","title":"抗滑摩擦與揚壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sliding friction and uplift: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「抗滑摩擦與揚壓」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sliding friction and uplift” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用總自重計摩擦會高估有揚壓時的抗滑能力。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對揚壓量測與接觸剪力試驗並分列各荷載組合，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using gross weight for friction overstates resistance when uplift acts. Diagnose it by the following check: Check measured uplift and interface shear testing and list load combinations separately. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「揚壓只影響抗浮而不影響滑動摩擦」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uplift affects flotation only and never sliding friction\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用總自重計摩擦會高估有揚壓時的抗滑能力。診斷時應採取以下查核：核對揚壓量測與接觸剪力試驗並分列各荷載組合，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Using gross weight for friction overstates resistance when uplift acts. Diagnose it by the following check: Check measured uplift and interface shear testing and list load combinations separately. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「抗滑摩擦與揚壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sliding friction and uplift\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["用總自重計摩擦會高估有揚壓時的抗滑能力。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","完全拘束彈性熱應力就是所有實際位置的應力"],"optionsEn":["Using gross weight for friction overstates resistance when uplift acts.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Fully restrained elastic thermal stress equals stress at every actual location"],"answer":0,"explanation":"用總自重計摩擦會高估有揚壓時的抗滑能力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using gross weight for friction overstates resistance when uplift acts. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b214-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「水化熱與拘束」與「帷幕試驗與滲透」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Hydration heat and restraint\" and \"Curtain testing and permeability\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b214-v15-25","title":"水化熱與拘束：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Hydration heat and restraint: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「水化熱與拘束」如何影響大迪克桑斯壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Hydration heat and restraint” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grande Dixence Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"大量混凝土的內外溫差與基礎拘束可形成熱應力，澆置分塊及降溫歷程影響開裂。單軸完全拘束且橫向可自由變形的線彈性公式只是應力量級，實際徐變、成熟度與裂縫會鬆弛應力；應用溫度與應變同步紀錄判斷，而非只量表面溫度。 驗證時應比較核心表面溫度與埋設應變並記錄混凝土齡期，並辨識以下失效情境：忽略徐變或拘束差異會使彈性熱應力被誤當實測值。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水化熱與拘束」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Mass concrete develops thermal stress through gradients and restraint. Block placement and cooling history affect cracking. An elastic estimate with full axial restraint and free lateral deformation gives a uniaxial stress scale only; creep, maturity and cracking relax stress. Interpret temperature and strain together rather than using surface temperature as the full thermal state. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare core and surface temperatures with embedded strain and concrete age. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Ignoring creep or restraint differences turns an elastic estimate into a false measured stress. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Hydration heat and restraint” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Uniaxial full axial restraint with free lateral deformation: E=25 GPa; alpha=10e-6 perK; cooling=12 K; elasticStress=25e9*10e-6*12/1e6=3 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Uniaxial full axial restraint with free lateral deformation: E=25 GPa; alpha=10e-6 perK; cooling=12 K; elasticStress=25e9*10e-6*12/1e6=3 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「完全拘束彈性熱應力就是所有實際位置的應力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Fully restrained elastic thermal stress equals stress at every actual location\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水化熱與拘束」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Hydration heat and restraint”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-25-k1","title":"水化熱與拘束","titleEn":"Hydration heat and restraint","text":"大量混凝土的內外溫差與基礎拘束可形成熱應力，澆置分塊及降溫歷程影響開裂。單軸完全拘束且橫向可自由變形的線彈性公式只是應力量級，實際徐變、成熟度與裂縫會鬆弛應力；應用溫度與應變同步紀錄判斷，而非只量表面溫度。","textEn":"Mass concrete develops thermal stress through gradients and restraint. Block placement and cooling history affect cracking.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：完全拘束彈性熱應力就是所有實際位置的應力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Fully restrained elastic thermal stress equals stress at every actual location Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水化熱與拘束」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Hydration heat and restraint\" is correct?","options":["完全拘束彈性熱應力就是所有實際位置的應力","大量混凝土的內外溫差與基礎拘束可形成熱應力，澆置分塊及降溫歷程影響開裂。","灌漿量越多就必定代表防滲效果越好"],"optionsEn":["Fully restrained elastic thermal stress equals stress at every actual location","Mass concrete develops thermal stress through gradients and restraint.","More injected grout necessarily means better seepage control"],"answer":1,"explanation":"大量混凝土的內外溫差與基礎拘束可形成熱應力，澆置分塊及降溫歷程影響開裂。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Mass concrete develops thermal stress through gradients and restraint. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b214-v15-26","title":"水化熱與拘束：定量估算","titleEn":"Hydration heat and restraint: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水化熱與拘束」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Hydration heat and restraint” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Uniaxial full axial restraint with free lateral deformation: E=25 GPa; alpha=10e-6 perK; cooling=12 K; elasticStress=25e9*10e-6*12/1e6=3 MPa。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Uniaxial full axial restraint with free lateral deformation: E=25 GPa; alpha=10e-6 perK; cooling=12 K; elasticStress=25e9*10e-6*12/1e6=3 MPa. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：比較核心表面溫度與埋設應變並記錄混凝土齡期。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare core and surface temperatures with embedded strain and concrete age.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Uniaxial full axial restraint with free lateral deformation: E=25 GPa; alpha=10e-6 perK; cooling=12 K; elasticStress=25e9*10e-6*12/1e6=3 MPa。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Uniaxial full axial restraint with free lateral deformation: E=25 GPa; alpha=10e-6 perK; cooling=12 K; elasticStress=25e9*10e-6*12/1e6=3 MPa. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水化熱與拘束」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Hydration heat and restraint\", which statement holds?","options":["壩高就是整個高山水電系統的總發電落差","公開壩高就是任何工況下的實際水深","原創教學假設：Uniaxial full axial restraint with free lateral deformation: E=25 GPa; alpha=10e-6 perK; cooling=12 K; elasticStress=25e9*10e-6*12/1e6=3 MPa。"],"optionsEn":["Dam height equals the full generating head of an alpine scheme","Published dam height equals actual water depth in every condition","Original teaching assumptions: Uniaxial full axial restraint with free lateral deformation: E=25 GPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Uniaxial full axial restraint with free lateral deformation: E=25 GPa; alpha=10e-6 perK; cooling=12 K; elasticStress=25e9*10e-6*12/1e6=3 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Uniaxial full axial restraint with free lateral deformation: E=25 GPa; alpha=10e-6 perK; cooling=12 K; elasticStress=25e9*10e-6*12/1e6=3 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b214-v15-27","title":"水化熱與拘束：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Hydration heat and restraint: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水化熱與拘束」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Hydration heat and restraint” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"比較核心表面溫度與埋設應變並記錄混凝土齡期。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「忽略徐變或拘束差異會使彈性熱應力被誤當實測值」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare core and surface temperatures with embedded strain and concrete age. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Ignoring creep or restraint differences turns an elastic estimate into a false measured stress. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以比較核心表面溫度與埋設應變並記錄混凝土齡期作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對忽略徐變或拘束差異會使彈性熱應力被誤當實測值，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare core and surface temperatures with embedded strain and concrete age. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Ignoring creep or restraint differences turns an elastic estimate into a false measured stress. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略徐變或拘束差異會使彈性熱應力被誤當實測值。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring creep or restraint differences turns an elastic estimate into a false measured stress. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"比較核心表面溫度與埋設應變並記錄混凝土齡期。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「忽略徐變或拘束差異會使彈性熱應力被誤當實測值」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare core and surface temperatures with embedded strain and concrete age. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Ignoring creep or restraint differences turns an elastic estimate into a false measured stress. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以比較核心表面溫度與埋設應變並記錄混凝土齡期作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對忽略徐變或拘束差異會使彈性熱應力被誤當實測值，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare core and surface temperatures with embedded strain and concrete age. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Ignoring creep or restraint differences turns an elastic estimate into a false measured stress. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水化熱與拘束」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Hydration heat and restraint\"?","options":["比較核心表面溫度與埋設應變並記錄混凝土齡期。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","一個排水孔壓力低就代表整個底面揚力低"],"optionsEn":["Compare core and surface temperatures with embedded strain and concrete age.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Low pressure at one drain proves low uplift across the entire base"],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較核心表面溫度與埋設應變並記錄混凝土齡期。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare core and surface temperatures with embedded strain and concrete age. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b214-v15-28","title":"水化熱與拘束：失效診斷","titleEn":"Hydration heat and restraint: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水化熱與拘束」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Hydration heat and restraint” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略徐變或拘束差異會使彈性熱應力被誤當實測值。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較核心表面溫度與埋設應變並記錄混凝土齡期，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring creep or restraint differences turns an elastic estimate into a false measured stress. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare core and surface temperatures with embedded strain and concrete age. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「完全拘束彈性熱應力就是所有實際位置的應力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Fully restrained elastic thermal stress equals stress at every actual location\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略徐變或拘束差異會使彈性熱應力被誤當實測值。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較核心表面溫度與埋設應變並記錄混凝土齡期，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Ignoring creep or restraint differences turns an elastic estimate into a false measured stress. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare core and surface temperatures with embedded strain and concrete age. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水化熱與拘束」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Hydration heat and restraint\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","忽略徐變或拘束差異會使彈性熱應力被誤當實測值。","灌漿量越多就必定代表防滲效果越好"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Ignoring creep or restraint differences turns an elastic estimate into a false measured stress.","More injected grout necessarily means better seepage control"],"answer":1,"explanation":"忽略徐變或拘束差異會使彈性熱應力被誤當實測值。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring creep or restraint differences turns an elastic estimate into a false measured stress. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b214-v15-29","title":"帷幕試驗與滲透：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Curtain testing and permeability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「帷幕試驗與滲透」如何影響大迪克桑斯壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Curtain testing and permeability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grande Dixence Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"灌漿帷幕應改變裂隙導水而非只追求灌入量，取芯、壓水與監測資料共同評估效果。前後流量比只能在同壓差及試段條件下比較，不能直接等同整壩滲透率降幅；地下水路重分配需靠廊道孔壓與流量追蹤。 驗證時應保持試段長度壓差一致並比較帷幕上下游孔壓，並辨識以下失效情境：只看灌漿量多會誤把遠處流失當有效封堵。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「帷幕試驗與滲透」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A grout curtain should alter fracture conductance, not merely absorb grout volume. Compare pressure tests, cores and monitoring. A before-and-after flow ratio requires matching test intervals and pressure; it does not directly equal whole-dam permeability reduction because pathways may redistribute through the foundation. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Match interval length and pressure and compare heads on both sides of the curtain. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Large grout take can represent loss elsewhere instead of effective sealing. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Curtain testing and permeability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Matched test pressure: initialWaterTake=20 L/min; finalWaterTake=5 L/min; observedReduction=(20-5)/20*100=75 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Matched test pressure: initialWaterTake=20 L/min; finalWaterTake=5 L/min; observedReduction=(20-5)/20*100=75 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「灌漿量越多就必定代表防滲效果越好」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"More injected grout necessarily means better seepage control\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「帷幕試驗與滲透」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Curtain testing and permeability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-29-k1","title":"帷幕試驗與滲透","titleEn":"Curtain testing and permeability","text":"灌漿帷幕應改變裂隙導水而非只追求灌入量，取芯、壓水與監測資料共同評估效果。前後流量比只能在同壓差及試段條件下比較，不能直接等同整壩滲透率降幅；地下水路重分配需靠廊道孔壓與流量追蹤。","textEn":"A grout curtain should alter fracture conductance, not merely absorb grout volume. Compare pressure tests, cores and monitoring.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：灌漿量越多就必定代表防滲效果越好 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: More injected grout necessarily means better seepage control Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「帷幕試驗與滲透」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Curtain testing and permeability\" is correct?","options":["灌漿量越多就必定代表防滲效果越好","垂線差值必定就是壩體絕對地理位移","灌漿帷幕應改變裂隙導水而非只追求灌入量，取芯、壓水與監測資料共同評估效果。"],"optionsEn":["More injected grout necessarily means better seepage control","A plumb-line difference necessarily equals absolute geographic dam movement","A grout curtain should alter fracture conductance, not merely absorb grout volume."],"answer":2,"explanation":"灌漿帷幕應改變裂隙導水而非只追求灌入量，取芯、壓水與監測資料共同評估效果。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A grout curtain should alter fracture conductance, not merely absorb grout volume. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b214-v15-30","title":"帷幕試驗與滲透：定量估算","titleEn":"Curtain testing and permeability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「帷幕試驗與滲透」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Curtain testing and permeability” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Matched test pressure: initialWaterTake=20 L/min; finalWaterTake=5 L/min; observedReduction=(20-5)/20*100=75 percent。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Matched test pressure: initialWaterTake=20 L/min; finalWaterTake=5 L/min; observedReduction=(20-5)/20*100=75 percent. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：保持試段長度壓差一致並比較帷幕上下游孔壓。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Match interval length and pressure and compare heads on both sides of the curtain.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Matched test pressure: initialWaterTake=20 L/min; finalWaterTake=5 L/min; observedReduction=(20-5)/20*100=75 percent。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Matched test pressure: initialWaterTake=20 L/min; finalWaterTake=5 L/min; observedReduction=(20-5)/20*100=75 percent. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「帷幕試驗與滲透」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Curtain testing and permeability\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：Matched test pressure: initialWaterTake=20 L/min; finalWaterTake=5 L/min; observedReduction=(20-5)/20*100=75 percent。","收集到的水量必定全部轉成可發電水量","混凝土質量的噸數可以直接當作千牛頓重量"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Matched test pressure: initialWaterTake=20 L/min; finalWaterTake=5 L/min; observedReduction=(20-5)/20*100=75 percent.","Every collected water volume necessarily becomes generating water","Concrete mass in tonnes can be used directly as weight in kilonewtons"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Matched test pressure: initialWaterTake=20 L/min; finalWaterTake=5 L/min; observedReduction=(20-5)/20*100=75 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Matched test pressure: initialWaterTake=20 L/min; finalWaterTake=5 L/min; observedReduction=(20-5)/20*100=75 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b214-v15-31","title":"帷幕試驗與滲透：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Curtain testing and permeability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「帷幕試驗與滲透」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Curtain testing and permeability” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"保持試段長度壓差一致並比較帷幕上下游孔壓。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只看灌漿量多會誤把遠處流失當有效封堵」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Match interval length and pressure and compare heads on both sides of the curtain. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Large grout take can represent loss elsewhere instead of effective sealing. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以保持試段長度壓差一致並比較帷幕上下游孔壓作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只看灌漿量多會誤把遠處流失當有效封堵，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Match interval length and pressure and compare heads on both sides of the curtain. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Large grout take can represent loss elsewhere instead of effective sealing. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：只看灌漿量多會誤把遠處流失當有效封堵。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Large grout take can represent loss elsewhere instead of effective sealing. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"保持試段長度壓差一致並比較帷幕上下游孔壓。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只看灌漿量多會誤把遠處流失當有效封堵」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Match interval length and pressure and compare heads on both sides of the curtain. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Large grout take can represent loss elsewhere instead of effective sealing. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以保持試段長度壓差一致並比較帷幕上下游孔壓作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只看灌漿量多會誤把遠處流失當有效封堵，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Match interval length and pressure and compare heads on both sides of the curtain. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Large grout take can represent loss elsewhere instead of effective sealing. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「帷幕試驗與滲透」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Curtain testing and permeability\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","保持試段長度壓差一致並比較帷幕上下游孔壓。","合力在底面內就保證全底面始終受壓"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Match interval length and pressure and compare heads on both sides of the curtain.","A resultant anywhere inside the base guarantees compression over the entire base"],"answer":1,"explanation":"保持試段長度壓差一致並比較帷幕上下游孔壓。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Match interval length and pressure and compare heads on both sides of the curtain. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b214-v15-32","title":"帷幕試驗與滲透：失效診斷","titleEn":"Curtain testing and permeability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「帷幕試驗與滲透」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Curtain testing and permeability” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只看灌漿量多會誤把遠處流失當有效封堵。診斷時應採取以下查核：保持試段長度壓差一致並比較帷幕上下游孔壓，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Large grout take can represent loss elsewhere instead of effective sealing. Diagnose it by the following check: Match interval length and pressure and compare heads on both sides of the curtain. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「灌漿量越多就必定代表防滲效果越好」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"More injected grout necessarily means better seepage control\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只看灌漿量多會誤把遠處流失當有效封堵。診斷時應採取以下查核：保持試段長度壓差一致並比較帷幕上下游孔壓，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Large grout take can represent loss elsewhere instead of effective sealing. Diagnose it by the following check: Match interval length and pressure and compare heads on both sides of the curtain. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「帷幕試驗與滲透」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Curtain testing and permeability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","垂線差值必定就是壩體絕對地理位移","只看灌漿量多會誤把遠處流失當有效封堵。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A plumb-line difference necessarily equals absolute geographic dam movement","Large grout take can represent loss elsewhere instead of effective sealing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只看灌漿量多會誤把遠處流失當有效封堵。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Large grout take can represent loss elsewhere instead of effective sealing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b214-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「垂線位移與溫度」與「高落差輸水與淨能量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Plumb-line movement and temperature\" and \"High-head conveyance and net energy\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b214-v15-33","title":"垂線位移與溫度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Plumb-line movement and temperature: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「垂線位移與溫度」如何影響大迪克桑斯壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Plumb-line movement and temperature” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grande Dixence Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"壩內垂線與外部測量可追蹤壩體位移，但基準點穩定與溫度水位效應需分開。差值代表相對運動而非絕對地盤移動，參考端本身若漂移需額外控制；應用長期可逆模式辨認新的不可逆殘差。 驗證時應以外部控制網與倒垂線比較基準穩定並核對季節循環，並辨識以下失效情境：基準端移動可使壩體看似發生相反方向位移。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「垂線位移與溫度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Internal plumb lines and external surveys track movement, but reference stability and temperature-stage effects need separation. A difference is relative motion, not absolute ground movement. If the reference moves, independent control is needed; use reversible long-term patterns to identify a new irreversible residual. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare reference stability using external control and inverted plumb lines and check seasonal cycles. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Reference movement can make the dam appear to move in the opposite direction. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Plumb-line movement and temperature” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：MeasuredRelativeDisplacement=18 mm; temperatureStageBaseline=13 mm; residual=18-13=5 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: MeasuredRelativeDisplacement=18 mm; temperatureStageBaseline=13 mm; residual=18-13=5 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「垂線差值必定就是壩體絕對地理位移」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A plumb-line difference necessarily equals absolute geographic dam movement\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「垂線位移與溫度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Plumb-line movement and temperature”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-33-k1","title":"垂線位移與溫度","titleEn":"Plumb-line movement and temperature","text":"壩內垂線與外部測量可追蹤壩體位移，但基準點穩定與溫度水位效應需分開。差值代表相對運動而非絕對地盤移動，參考端本身若漂移需額外控制；應用長期可逆模式辨認新的不可逆殘差。","textEn":"Internal plumb lines and external surveys track movement, but reference stability and temperature-stage effects need separation. A difference is relative motion, not absolute ground movement.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：垂線差值必定就是壩體絕對地理位移 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A plumb-line difference necessarily equals absolute geographic dam movement Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「垂線位移與溫度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Plumb-line movement and temperature\" is correct?","options":["壩內垂線與外部測量可追蹤壩體位移，但基準點穩定與溫度水位效應需分開。","垂線差值必定就是壩體絕對地理位移","壩高就是整個高山水電系統的總發電落差"],"optionsEn":["Internal plumb lines and external surveys track movement, but reference stability and temperature-stage effects need separation.","A plumb-line difference necessarily equals absolute geographic dam movement","Dam height equals the full generating head of an alpine scheme"],"answer":0,"explanation":"壩內垂線與外部測量可追蹤壩體位移，但基準點穩定與溫度水位效應需分開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Internal plumb lines and external surveys track movement, but reference stability and temperature-stage effects need separation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b214-v15-34","title":"垂線位移與溫度：定量估算","titleEn":"Plumb-line movement and temperature: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「垂線位移與溫度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Plumb-line movement and temperature” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：MeasuredRelativeDisplacement=18 mm; temperatureStageBaseline=13 mm; residual=18-13=5 mm。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: MeasuredRelativeDisplacement=18 mm; temperatureStageBaseline=13 mm; residual=18-13=5 mm. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以外部控制網與倒垂線比較基準穩定並核對季節循環。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare reference stability using external control and inverted plumb lines and check seasonal cycles.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：MeasuredRelativeDisplacement=18 mm; temperatureStageBaseline=13 mm; residual=18-13=5 mm。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: MeasuredRelativeDisplacement=18 mm; temperatureStageBaseline=13 mm; residual=18-13=5 mm. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「垂線位移與溫度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Plumb-line movement and temperature\", which statement holds?","options":["公開壩高就是任何工況下的實際水深","原創教學假設：MeasuredRelativeDisplacement=18 mm; temperatureStageBaseline=13 mm; residual=18-13=5 mm。","一個排水孔壓力低就代表整個底面揚力低"],"optionsEn":["Published dam height equals actual water depth in every condition","Original teaching assumptions: MeasuredRelativeDisplacement=18 mm; temperatureStageBaseline=13 mm; residual=18-13=5 mm.","Low pressure at one drain proves low uplift across the entire base"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：MeasuredRelativeDisplacement=18 mm; temperatureStageBaseline=13 mm; residual=18-13=5 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: MeasuredRelativeDisplacement=18 mm; temperatureStageBaseline=13 mm; residual=18-13=5 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b214-v15-35","title":"垂線位移與溫度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Plumb-line movement and temperature: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「垂線位移與溫度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Plumb-line movement and temperature” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以外部控制網與倒垂線比較基準穩定並核對季節循環。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「基準端移動可使壩體看似發生相反方向位移」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare reference stability using external control and inverted plumb lines and check seasonal cycles. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Reference movement can make the dam appear to move in the opposite direction. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以外部控制網與倒垂線比較基準穩定並核對季節循環作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對基準端移動可使壩體看似發生相反方向位移，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare reference stability using external control and inverted plumb lines and check seasonal cycles. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Reference movement can make the dam appear to move in the opposite direction. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：基準端移動可使壩體看似發生相反方向位移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Reference movement can make the dam appear to move in the opposite direction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以外部控制網與倒垂線比較基準穩定並核對季節循環。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「基準端移動可使壩體看似發生相反方向位移」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare reference stability using external control and inverted plumb lines and check seasonal cycles. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Reference movement can make the dam appear to move in the opposite direction. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以外部控制網與倒垂線比較基準穩定並核對季節循環作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對基準端移動可使壩體看似發生相反方向位移，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare reference stability using external control and inverted plumb lines and check seasonal cycles. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Reference movement can make the dam appear to move in the opposite direction. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「垂線位移與溫度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Plumb-line movement and temperature\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","揚壓只影響抗浮而不影響滑動摩擦","以外部控制網與倒垂線比較基準穩定並核對季節循環。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uplift affects flotation only and never sliding friction","Compare reference stability using external control and inverted plumb lines and check seasonal cycles."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以外部控制網與倒垂線比較基準穩定並核對季節循環。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare reference stability using external control and inverted plumb lines and check seasonal cycles. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b214-v15-36","title":"垂線位移與溫度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Plumb-line movement and temperature: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「垂線位移與溫度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Plumb-line movement and temperature” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"基準端移動可使壩體看似發生相反方向位移。診斷時應採取以下查核：以外部控制網與倒垂線比較基準穩定並核對季節循環，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Reference movement can make the dam appear to move in the opposite direction. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare reference stability using external control and inverted plumb lines and check seasonal cycles. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「垂線差值必定就是壩體絕對地理位移」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A plumb-line difference necessarily equals absolute geographic dam movement\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"基準端移動可使壩體看似發生相反方向位移。診斷時應採取以下查核：以外部控制網與倒垂線比較基準穩定並核對季節循環，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Reference movement can make the dam appear to move in the opposite direction. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare reference stability using external control and inverted plumb lines and check seasonal cycles. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「垂線位移與溫度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Plumb-line movement and temperature\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["基準端移動可使壩體看似發生相反方向位移。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","壩高就是整個高山水電系統的總發電落差"],"optionsEn":["Reference movement can make the dam appear to move in the opposite direction.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Dam height equals the full generating head of an alpine scheme"],"answer":0,"explanation":"基準端移動可使壩體看似發生相反方向位移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Reference movement can make the dam appear to move in the opposite direction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b214-v15-37","title":"高落差輸水與淨能量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"High-head conveyance and net energy: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「高落差輸水與淨能量」如何影響大迪克桑斯壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “High-head conveyance and net energy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grande Dixence Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"高山蓄水到低處電廠的高程差提供勢能，輸水損失與抽水投入則影響淨能量。以指定流量與淨水頭估出力只代表單一工作點，不能把壩高等同全系統落差；水路壓力、暫態與機組效率需另作聯合驗證。 驗證時應同步核對上下游能量線機組功率及抽水投入，並辨識以下失效情境：把發電毛能量當淨收益會漏掉抽水與輸水損失。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「高落差輸水與淨能量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Elevation difference from alpine storage to lower generating plants supplies potential energy, while losses and pumping inputs affect net benefit. Power at specified flow and net head is one operating point. Dam height is not total scheme head; waterway pressures, transients and efficiency require joint verification. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Check energy lines, generating power and pumping input over matching periods. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Treating gross generation as net benefit omits pumping input and conveyance losses. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “High-head conveyance and net energy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：HypotheticalQ=25 m3/s; netHead=900 m; efficiency=0.92; power=1000*9.81*25*900*0.92/1e6=203.067 MW。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalQ=25 m3/s; netHead=900 m; efficiency=0.92; power=1000*9.81*25*900*0.92/1e6=203.067 MW.","failure":"常見誤解：「壩高就是整個高山水電系統的總發電落差」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Dam height equals the full generating head of an alpine scheme\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「高落差輸水與淨能量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “High-head conveyance and net energy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-37-k1","title":"高落差輸水與淨能量","titleEn":"High-head conveyance and net energy","text":"高山蓄水到低處電廠的高程差提供勢能，輸水損失與抽水投入則影響淨能量。以指定流量與淨水頭估出力只代表單一工作點，不能把壩高等同全系統落差；水路壓力、暫態與機組效率需另作聯合驗證。","textEn":"Elevation difference from alpine storage to lower generating plants supplies potential energy, while losses and pumping inputs affect net benefit. Power at specified flow and net head is one operating point.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：壩高就是整個高山水電系統的總發電落差 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Dam height equals the full generating head of an alpine scheme Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高落差輸水與淨能量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"High-head conveyance and net energy\" is correct?","options":["壩高就是整個高山水電系統的總發電落差","高山蓄水到低處電廠的高程差提供勢能，輸水損失與抽水投入則影響淨能量。","收集到的水量必定全部轉成可發電水量"],"optionsEn":["Dam height equals the full generating head of an alpine scheme","Elevation difference from alpine storage to lower generating plants supplies potential energy, while losses and pumping inputs affect net benefit.","Every collected water volume necessarily becomes generating water"],"answer":1,"explanation":"高山蓄水到低處電廠的高程差提供勢能，輸水損失與抽水投入則影響淨能量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Elevation difference from alpine storage to lower generating plants supplies potential energy, while losses and pumping inputs affect net benefit. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b214-v15-38","title":"高落差輸水與淨能量：定量估算","titleEn":"High-head conveyance and net energy: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「高落差輸水與淨能量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “High-head conveyance and net energy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：HypotheticalQ=25 m3/s; netHead=900 m; efficiency=0.92; power=1000*9.81*25*900*0.92/1e6=203.067 MW。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalQ=25 m3/s; netHead=900 m; efficiency=0.92; power=1000*9.81*25*900*0.92/1e6=203.067 MW. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步核對上下游能量線機組功率及抽水投入。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check energy lines, generating power and pumping input over matching periods.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：HypotheticalQ=25 m3/s; netHead=900 m; efficiency=0.92; power=1000*9.81*25*900*0.92/1e6=203.067 MW。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalQ=25 m3/s; netHead=900 m; efficiency=0.92; power=1000*9.81*25*900*0.92/1e6=203.067 MW. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「高落差輸水與淨能量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"High-head conveyance and net energy\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土質量的噸數可以直接當作千牛頓重量","合力在底面內就保證全底面始終受壓","原創教學假設：HypotheticalQ=25 m3/s; netHead=900 m; efficiency=0.92; power=1000*9.81*25*900*0.92/1e6=203.067 MW。"],"optionsEn":["Concrete mass in tonnes can be used directly as weight in kilonewtons","A resultant anywhere inside the base guarantees compression over the entire base","Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalQ=25 m3/s; netHead=900 m; efficiency=0.92; power=1000*9.81*25*900*0.92/1e6=203.067 MW."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：HypotheticalQ=25 m3/s; netHead=900 m; efficiency=0.92; power=1000*9.81*25*900*0.92/1e6=203.067 MW。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalQ=25 m3/s; netHead=900 m; efficiency=0.92; power=1000*9.81*25*900*0.92/1e6=203.067 MW. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b214-v15-39","title":"高落差輸水與淨能量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"High-head conveyance and net energy: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「高落差輸水與淨能量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “High-head conveyance and net energy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步核對上下游能量線機組功率及抽水投入。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把發電毛能量當淨收益會漏掉抽水與輸水損失」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check energy lines, generating power and pumping input over matching periods. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Treating gross generation as net benefit omits pumping input and conveyance losses. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以同步核對上下游能量線機組功率及抽水投入作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把發電毛能量當淨收益會漏掉抽水與輸水損失，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check energy lines, generating power and pumping input over matching periods. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Treating gross generation as net benefit omits pumping input and conveyance losses. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：把發電毛能量當淨收益會漏掉抽水與輸水損失。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating gross generation as net benefit omits pumping input and conveyance losses. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步核對上下游能量線機組功率及抽水投入。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「把發電毛能量當淨收益會漏掉抽水與輸水損失」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Check energy lines, generating power and pumping input over matching periods. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Treating gross generation as net benefit omits pumping input and conveyance losses. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以同步核對上下游能量線機組功率及抽水投入作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對把發電毛能量當淨收益會漏掉抽水與輸水損失，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check energy lines, generating power and pumping input over matching periods. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Treating gross generation as net benefit omits pumping input and conveyance losses. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「高落差輸水與淨能量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"High-head conveyance and net energy\"?","options":["同步核對上下游能量線機組功率及抽水投入。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","完全拘束彈性熱應力就是所有實際位置的應力"],"optionsEn":["Check energy lines, generating power and pumping input over matching periods.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Fully restrained elastic thermal stress equals stress at every actual location"],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步核對上下游能量線機組功率及抽水投入。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check energy lines, generating power and pumping input over matching periods. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b214-v15-40","title":"高落差輸水與淨能量：失效診斷","titleEn":"High-head conveyance and net energy: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"prerequisiteIds":["b214-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「高落差輸水與淨能量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “High-head conveyance and net energy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把發電毛能量當淨收益會漏掉抽水與輸水損失。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步核對上下游能量線機組功率及抽水投入，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating gross generation as net benefit omits pumping input and conveyance losses. Diagnose it by the following check: Check energy lines, generating power and pumping input over matching periods. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「壩高就是整個高山水電系統的總發電落差」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Dam height equals the full generating head of an alpine scheme\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b214-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把發電毛能量當淨收益會漏掉抽水與輸水損失。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步核對上下游能量線機組功率及抽水投入，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Treating gross generation as net benefit omits pumping input and conveyance losses. Diagnose it by the following check: Check energy lines, generating power and pumping input over matching periods. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]},{"id":"b214-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高落差輸水與淨能量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"High-head conveyance and net energy\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","把發電毛能量當淨收益會漏掉抽水與輸水損失。","收集到的水量必定全部轉成可發電水量"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Treating gross generation as net benefit omits pumping input and conveyance losses.","Every collected water volume necessarily becomes generating water"],"answer":1,"explanation":"把發電毛能量當淨收益會漏掉抽水與輸水損失。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating gross generation as net benefit omits pumping input and conveyance losses. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","v15s-grande-dixence-owner","v15s-grande-dixence-history","v15s-usbr-monitoring","v15s-usace-hss"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
